note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note bridge/cuda/gate.om: BRIDGE-CUDA, the gate of the CUDA compatibility profile moved from CUDApp compat/cuda,
note in seeded Omega (Linux AArch64). Build from the repository root (OM-2 program mode; seed/ng/sha256.om supplies
note sh_dat, sh_all, sh_dig, sh_hexd):
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/ng/sha256.om bridge/cuda/gate.om; } | seed/out/omc > gate
note Run from the repository root:
note   gate SCRATCH C0CHECK FIXTURE [CUDAPP OLDOMC CC_AARCH64 CC_X86_64]
note SCRATCH  a new directory (made 0700); an existing one is refused (exit 2). It must be absolute (start with /)
note          when the oracle tier runs: build.sh builds in absolute directories.
note C0CHECK  bridge/cuda/c0_check.om built after gpu/nvidia/om/cache/digest.om
note FIXTURE  bridge/cuda/fixture.om built
note Tier A (always): the work of CUDApp compat/cuda/test.sh at 84b524ca, with the executables and the PTX made by
note FIXTURE instead of by gcc and build.sh. FIXTURE writes the PTX, and synthesizes both executables twice from
note bridge/cuda/fixture-ISA.tsv (the profile reader's own view of the gcc executables): the two builds must hold
note the same bytes, and C0CHECK emit on the synthetic executable must give the table again, line for line after
note the first (the first line is the artifact row, which names the executable's own digest). The v3 profiles
note are then re-pinned to the synthetic digests, and the 16 checks of test.sh run with the same mutations. Their
note transcript, without the two "built ISA" lines whose digests name gcc's executables, must equal lines 3 to the
note end of bridge/cuda/test-sh-84b524ca.txt, the output of test.sh at CUDApp 84b524ca.
note Tier B (oracle, only with the four optional arguments, all absolute paths): runs CUDAPP/compat/cuda/test.sh
note with OMEGA_OMC=OLDOMC (the compiler that test pins) and PATH=/usr/bin:/bin; its output must equal the whole
note transcript file. Then builds vadd_drv for each ISA as build.sh does, but links it against the libcuda.so.1
note stub made by FIXTURE: the executable must have the digest pinned in the v3 profile. Then C0CHECK emit of the
note test's own executables must equal the fixture tables, and of its no-libcuda executable the synthetic one.
note Then (tier A, outside the transcript) the limit check: three profile versions of 16777215 bytes together are
note read and compared, of 16777216 refused; and every file named in bridge/cuda/copied.tsv must have its digest
note (tier B checks CUDAPP/compat/cuda's files against the same table). Transcript lines 1-2 (gcc's hashes) are
note compared only by tier B.
note Output: one line per check, then BRIDGE-CUDA PASS|FAIL checks=N failed=F oracle=PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN
note hardware=NOT_RUN. The device run of vadd_drv (VADD_U32 PASS on a GPU) is never made here.
note Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 bad usage or setup. Buffers: files up to 16 MiB, captured outputs up to 1 MiB, paths
note up to 4096 bytes; anything larger is a FAIL or exit 2, never truncated.
